# <type>[optional scope]: <description>
# |<----  Limit to 50 characters  ---->|

# Explain why this change is being made
# |<----   Wrap at 72 characters   ---->|

# Provide links to relevant issues
# Closes #
# Fixes #
# Refs #

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be (same list as the commit-msg hook and pr-title.yml):
#   feat     (new feature)
#   fix      (bug fix)
#   docs     (documentation)
#   style    (formatting, no code change)
#   refactor (refactoring)
#   perf     (performance)
#   test     (tests)
#   build    (build system or dependencies)
#   ci       (CI configuration and scripts)
#   chore    (other maintenance)
#   revert   (revert a previous commit)
# --------------------
# Scopes (NAILS-specific):
#   core, cli, ci, nix, e2e, release, docs, deps
# --------------------
# Remember:
#   - Use imperative mood ("add" not "added")
#   - Don't end subject with period
#   - Separate subject from body with blank line
#   - Release bumps use chore(release): ...
# --------------------
# Examples:
#   feat(cli): add lazy build pattern
#   fix(core): prevent double-mount error
#   test(core): add property-based validation
#   chore(release): v0.3.0
